{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>And he split wood for the burnt-offering.</b> This shows his zeal in the commandment — for perhaps no wood would be found in that place, so he brought it along for three days. Or perhaps Abraham would disqualify any wood in which a worm was found, according to the Torah's rule, and therefore took from his house good wood fit for a burnt-offering, and concerning this it says ויבקע עצי עולה. R. Berakhiah said: In the merit that Abraham split wood for a burnt-offering, the Holy One, blessed be He, merited to split the sea for his children, as it says (Exodus 14:21) ״ויבקעו המים״. R. Levi said to him: It is enough for you, Berakhiah; rather, Abraham according to his ability and the Holy One, blessed be He, according to His ability. Thus far in Bereshit Rabbah."], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:14:03.349034756Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}